`placeOrder` validates every line against current menu availability and the restaurant's accept-orders capacity before committing anything:

```java
Order placeOrder(String restaurantId, List<OrderLine> lines) {
    Restaurant restaurant = restaurantRepo.get(restaurantId);
    if (!restaurant.isAcceptingOrders()) {
        throw new RestaurantUnavailableException();
    }
    for (OrderLine line : lines) {
        if (!restaurant.getMenuItem(line.getItemId()).isAvailable()) {
            throw new ItemUnavailableException(line.getItemId());
        }
    }
    Order order = new Order(restaurantId, lines, Status.PLACED);
    orderRepo.save(order);
    return order;
}
```

Validating every line before saving anything avoids the awkward case of a half-valid order sitting in PLACED with one item that can never actually be prepared.
